{
 "brief": "An American writer, artist, and anthropologist of Armenian descent, Dana Marashvian, has dedicated a separate chapter to the Palestinian genocide in Gaza within her illustrated book \"The Book of Genocides,\" Shehab Wire reported. The volume was published by a university press and examines mass atrocities across regions and time periods.\n\nMarashvian's inclusion of Gaza reflects growing international documentation of the 2023-2024 conflict, which has killed tens of thousands and displaced millions of Palestinians. The illustrated format aims to make genocide documentation accessible to broader audiences beyond academic circles.",
